  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry you missed the Q4 planning invite. I checked your account and your spam quarantine. Your account looks fine, your mailbox has plenty of space, and the invite isn't stuck in spam. Here's what to try next:\n1. Sign in to Outlook on the web and check whether the meeting shows up on your calendar there. If it shows on the web but not in the Outlook app on your laptop, please tell us. That points to a sync problem, and we have steps for it.\n2. Does anyone, such as an assistant, manage your calendar for you? If so, the invite may have gone only to them. Let us know and we can help change the settings so you get copies too.\n3. Ask the meeting organizer to send the invite to you again.\nPlease reply with what you find, and tell us who organized the meeting. If you also seem to miss other emails or invites from that same person, mention that too.",
  "internal_note": "User: Sofia Rossi (id 7), Marketing, account active, not VIP, mailbox 27.9% used. Following KB-012: spam quarantine is empty, so the invite was not quarantined. I have no tool to check delegate settings or compare web vs. desktop, so I asked the user about delegates and Outlook on the web and told her to ask the organizer to resend. If the web calendar is correct and only the desktop app is wrong, follow KB-009 (Outlook sync). Escalate to Tier 2 if invites from one specific internal organizer never arrive (possible mail rule or transport issue, per KB-012). Waiting for the organizer's name and the user's results.",
